            "kind": "execute",
            "status": "completed",
            "title": "cd flare_forecast sed -n '1,80p' configs/config_script.yaml",
            "raw_output": "# =============================================================================\n# Surya workshop \u2014 template fine-tuning config\n#\n# Five sections own all parameters:\n#   data      \u2014 what to load and how to align labels\n#   model     \u2014 backbone architecture, fine-tuning head, LoRA\n#   training  \u2014 optimization and augmentation hyperparameters\n#   output    \u2014 where to save checkpoints (and optional S3 upload)\n#   logging   \u2014 experiment tracking (WandB)\n#\n# Two things to know before editing:\n#\n#   * Paths are relative to THIS FILE's directory (~ and $ENV_VARS are expanded), so a\n#     fork works on any machine with no absolute paths to fix up. The one exception is\n#     s3_cache_dir \u2014 see its comment below.\n#   * Unrecognized keys are an ERROR, not a silent no-op. To add a task-specific key,\n#     add the field to your DataConfig subclass in configs.py first.\n#\n# Usage \u2014 --config defaults to this file, so the short form is enough:\n#   CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0,1 python -m downstream_apps.template.3_finetune_template_1D\n#\n# Per-run overrides that do not require editing this file:\n#   --max-epochs 5     --batch-size 4     --s3-cache-dir /scratch/$USER/cache\n#   --deterministic warn   (reproducible run; see training.deterministic below)\n# =============================================================================\n\njob_id: solar_flare_forecasting\n\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Data\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndata:\n  # -- Paths (relative to this file's directory) --\n  train_data_path: ../../../data/indices/surya_aws_s3_train.csv\n  valid_data_path: ../../../data/indices/surya_aws_s3_val.csv\n  scalers_path: ../assets/scalers.yaml\n\n  # -- Input channels and temporal sampling --\n  channels: [aia94, aia131, aia171, aia193, aia211, aia304, aia335, aia1600,\n             hmi_m, hmi_bx, hmi_by, hmi_bz, hmi_v]\n  time_delta_input_minutes: [-60, -36]   # Offsets (minutes) of input frames relative to reference timestep\n  time_delta_target_minutes: 0   # Step size (minutes) between forecast frames\n\n  # -- Downstream label alignment (flare catalog \u2192 Surya index) --\n  flare_index_path: ../data/hek_flare_catalog.csv\n#  ds_time_column: start_time      # Column in the flare catalog used as the event timestamp\n  ds_time_column: peak_time      # Column in the flare catalog used as the event timestamp\n  ds_time_tolerance: 24m           # Max allowed gap between catalog and Surya timestamps\n  ds_match_direction: forward     # \"forward\": use solar state *before* the flare (causal)\n\n  # -- Local data (only needed when the index contains relative local paths) --\n  # sdo_data_root_path: /path/to/sdo   # Prepended to relative local paths; ignored for s3://\n\n  # -- S3 (only needed when index contains s3:// paths) --\n  s3_anon: true                   # true for public buckets; false to use IAM credentials\n\n  # How S3 objects are read. Measured on one 13-channel SDO sample from\n  # s3://nasa-surya-bench (times are indicative, not a benchmark):\n  #\n  #   download    \u2014 fetch the whole file into s3_cache_dir, then open locally.\n  #                 ~9 s from a warm cache. Recommended, and the default.\n  #   simplecache \u2014 fsspec read-through cache into s3_cache_dir. ~29 s on a cold fetch.\n  #   stream      \u2014 read directly from S3, nothing written to disk, no cache dir needed.\n  #                 ~271 s \u2014 roughly 9x slower than just fetching the whole file, because\n  #                 HDF5 random access becomes many small ranged GETs. Use only when you\n  #                 cannot spare the disk.\n  s3_mode: download\n\n  # Local cache directory. REQUIRED unless s3_mode is \"stream\" \u2014 budget ~1 GB per unique\n  # timestep, so the right location depends on your machine's scratch space.\n  #\n  # Left null here on purpose: this file is checked in and shared, and an absolute path\n  # into one person's home is wrong for everyone else. Set it one of three ways\n  # (highest precedence first):\n  #\n  #   1. --s3-cache-dir /scratch/$USER/helio_cache   (per-run)\n  #   2. s3_cache_dir: /scratch/me/helio_cache       (here, in your own fork)\n  #   3. export SURYA_WS_CACHE_DIR=/scratch/me/helio_cache   (per-machine, config stays clean)\n  #\nShell cwd was reset to /home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/workshop_infrastructure/models",
