      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "Direct answers:\n\n**Yes, re-run it \u2014 but change two things first, or you'll hit the same wall.** The reason it \"wasn't fast\": you're at **~47 s/step**, and 55 steps \u00d7 47 s \u2248 **43 minutes** against a `max_time` budget of 45. It was never going to comfortably finish. And ~97% of that time is *not* GPU work \u2014 the GPU sat at 0% between 1\u20132 s bursts. You're bottlenecked on S3 reads of 13-channel 4096\u00d74096 NetCDF files (3 frames per sample: 2 inputs at \u221260/\u221236 min + 1 target).\n\nOne thing decides how fast a re-run is, so let me check it:",
