      "id": "82bdc804-0814-474a-9449-55f24794d281",
      "body": "Now the real diagnosis, and it's different from my first read:\n\n- **297 files were downloaded during your run** \u2014 the cache is big but holds mostly 2011\u20132013 files from earlier work, not the years this experiment picked (random train years, 2014\u201315 val, 2023 test). So you *were* fetching from S3.\n- Each frame is **~564 MB**, and you need **3 per sample** (~1.7 GB/sample).\n- Your cache sits on **EFS/NFS at 301 MB/s** \u2014 so even a *warm* sample costs ~6 s just to read bytes, before decode and normalization.\n- `s3_boto3_max_concurrency: 4` with only **4 loader workers** \u2014 that's your ceiling.\n\nLast lookup: I want the dataset's own download helper so the prefetch reuses it instead of me guessing your cache's `bucket__hash__file.nc` naming.",
