          "id": "opus[1m]",
          "settings": {
            "fast": "on"
          }
        }
      },
      "body": "ok. thanks but im confused. what's the solution here? what should i do and in what order?",
      "time": 1789671886.3429735,
      "type": "msg"
    },
    {
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "type": "msg",
      "raw_time": false,
      "time": 1789671908.2037108,
      "id": "a6674b25-2136-4310-9f7a-7cfee6b5c778",
      "body": "Two phases. Phase A gets you presentation material in ~15 minutes. Phase B is the clean run, only if time allows.\n\n## Phase A \u2014 salvage what you have (do this now)\n\n**1. Lock in the weights** (they're only in memory; an interrupt loses them):\n```python\ntrainer.save_checkpoint(\"interrupted_33steps.ckpt\")\nimport wandb\nif wandb.run is not None: wandb.run.finish()\n```\n\n**2. Run your existing Stage 4 cell** as-is. `lit_model` = 33 steps of fine-tuning, `df_baseline` = untrained control from 18:12. That's a valid before/after. ~4\u20136 min (val/test frames are warm from the baseline pass).\n\n**3. Run the Stage 4b plot cell** I gave you. That's your visual: last input | ground truth | prediction | error, with `skill` in each title.\n\nStop there. You have numbers + images + an honest label: *\"1 epoch, 33 of 55 steps, LoRA rank 8.\"*\n\n## Phase B \u2014 the clean 55-step run (only if you have an hour)\n\n**4.** Add `StepProgress()` to `Trainer(callbacks=[...])` and swap in the fixed status cell. Without this you're blind again.\n\n**5.** In cell 4: `LOADER_WORKERS = 8`, and `persistent_workers=True` in `make_loader`.\n\n**6.** In cell 14: `max_time={\"minutes\": 120}` (45 was below the ~43 min the run needs \u2014 that's the actual reason it was doomed).\n\n**7.** Re-run cells 5, 6, 7, 10 to rebuild the model fresh. Skipping this means training on top of the existing 33 steps with a fresh optimizer \u2014 muddled, not a clean 55.\n\n**8.** Re-run the fit cell. Watch `tail -f downstream_apps/flare_forecast/train_progress.log` in a terminal.\n\n**9.** Re-run Stage 4 + 4b.\n\nThe prefetch cell is optional \u2014 it helps most if you later scale past 87 flares. At this size, steps 5\u20136 are enough.\n\n## The two things that bit you tonight\n\n- **\"Idle\" kernel was a lie** \u2014 a dropped websocket froze the output while training ran fine. `train_progress.log` fixes that permanently.\n- **`max_time=45` couldn't fit a ~43 min run**, and the status cell then misreported your interrupt as the guard firing.",
