      "sender": "jpereira"
    },
    {
      "body": "That output is good. Three things in it confirm the run is set up correctly:\n\n- **`5.8 M Trainable params / 366 M Non-trainable / 371 M Total`** \u2014 identical to your earlier run. LoRA attached the same way, so this run is comparable to your baseline.\n- **`[19:40:54] START 32 steps -> train_progress.log`** \u2014 `StepProgress` is live, and it confirms 32 steps (your new `N_TRAIN`).\n- **`Skipping val loop`** \u2014 expected; you pass no val loader on purpose.\n\n**Ignore `Training: | 0/? [00:00<?, ?it/s]`.** That is the exact frozen tqdm bar that fooled you at 18:24. It will likely never update. It is not a status indicator.\n\n## What to watch instead\n\nLines like this, roughly one per step:\n\n```\n[19:41:38] step   1/32  loss 0.2314  compute   3.1s  data-wait  40.2s   44.0s/step  ETA 22.7m\n```\n\nThe first one takes longest \u2014 8 workers have to spawn and fill their prefetch queues, so give it 1\u20132 minutes before worrying. From a terminal:\n\n```\ntail -f /home/jovyan/tmp/surya_workshop/downstream_apps/flare_forecast/train_progress.log\n```\n\nRead `data-wait` on the first few lines to know your regime:\n\n| `data-wait` | meaning | 32-step ETA |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~35\u201345 s | cold S3 fetches | ~25 min |\n| ~10\u201315 s | warm EFS cache | ~8 min |\n| ~0\u20133 s | GPU-bound at last | ~3 min |\n\n`max_time` is 60 min, so even the cold case finishes with room. And the `ETA` column tells you directly \u2014 no more guessing.\n\nTwo harmless warnings: the `persistent_workers=True` suggestion (cosmetic), and `WANDB_NOTEBOOK_NAME ... 2b_flip_minimal.ipynb` (cell 1 still names the old file; it only affects wandb's metadata).\n\nOne real-but-not-blocking note: `538 module(s) in eval mode` / `0 Modules in train mode` means dropout is inactive during training, including your LoRA dropout of 0.1. That was true of your earlier run too, so it doesn't affect comparability with the baseline \u2014 just don't describe the run as using dropout regularization.",
