    {
      "id": "9da8c344-b6e3-4114-9ab4-25f968b4f35c",
      "mentions": [],
      "body": "Yes to both, but with two fixes.\n\n## 1. The status cell \u2014 use the corrected version\n\nYours hardcodes `45` in the message and blames `max_time` for *any* shortfall, which is exactly what misled you at 18:45. Replace it:\n\n```python\nexpected = trainer.max_epochs * len(train_data_loader)\nstatus = str(trainer.state.status)\nprint(\"status         :\", status)\nprint(\"epochs done    :\", trainer.current_epoch, \"of\", trainer.max_epochs)\nprint(\"optimizer steps:\", trainer.global_step, \"of\", expected)\nif \"INTERRUPTED\" in status.upper():\n    print(\"  ^^ interrupted by you / kernel restart -- max_time did NOT fire\")\nelif trainer.global_step < expected:\n    print(\"  ^^ stopped early -- the max_time guard fired\")\nelse:\n    print(\"  ^^ completed all steps\")\nprint(\"checkpoint     :\", trainer.checkpoint_callback.last_model_path or \"(none written)\")\n```\n\nYou want to see `FINISHED` and `32 of 32`.\n\n## 2. The save cell \u2014 change the filename first\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f **As written it will overwrite `interrupted_33steps.ckpt`** \u2014 your salvage fallback from the interrupted run. Don't destroy it. Use a new name:\n\n```python\ntrainer.save_checkpoint(\"finetuned_32steps.ckpt\")\nimport wandb\nif wandb.run is not None: wandb.run.finish()\n```\n\nAlso note the manual save is now just insurance: if the run reaches `FINISHED`, `save_last=True` writes `last.ckpt` at epoch end on its own, and the status cell will print that path. Cheap to do anyway.\n\n## Order once it finishes\n\n1. Fixed status cell \u2192 confirm `FINISHED`, `32 of 32`\n2. Save under the new name + `wandb.run.finish()`\n3. **Stage 4** \u2014 `df_baseline` is already in memory since you re-ran Stage 1 this session, so no CSV reload needed\n4. **Stage 4b** \u2014 the plots\n\nWhile you wait, `tail -f train_progress.log` and check the `data-wait` column on the first couple of steps \u2014 that tells you whether you're looking at ~8 minutes or ~25.",
      "time": 1789674257.4122152,
      "type": "msg",
      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false
    },
    {
      "sender": "jpereira",
