      "time": 1789675015.1625059,
      "body": "**Yes, it's done.** Three lines prove it:\n\n- `step 32/32` at 19:55:38\n- **`Trainer.fit stopped: max_epochs=1 reached.`** \u2014 Lightning's own clean-completion message. Not `max_time`, not an interrupt.\n- All 32 steps logged, none missing.\n\nIgnore `END status=TrainerStatus.RUNNING`. That's a quirk of my callback: `on_train_end` fires *during* fit teardown, before Lightning flips the status to `FINISHED`. Your status cell is the authority \u2014 run it and it will say `FINISHED`, `32 of 32`.\n\n## Where the 14.7 minutes went\n\n| | time | share |\n|---|---|---|\n| worker spawn + first batch | 209 s | 24% |\n| `data-wait` stalls (8 cold fetches) | ~591 s | 67% |\n| **actual GPU compute** (32 \u00d7 2.1 s) | **67 s** | **7.5%** |\n\n`compute` was 2.1 s on every single step \u2014 the GPU is perfectly consistent. The sawtooth is entirely cold S3 fetches at steps 9, 10, 13, 17, 18, 25, 26. **That's your overnight lever:** run the prefetch cell first and you delete ~10 of those 14.7 minutes.\n\n## The loss, honestly\n\n`0.2269 \u2192 0.2123`, bouncing between 0.196 and 0.579, mean ~0.26. **No trend.** 32 steps at batch size 1 isn't enough to see learning, so don't claim improvement from this. Stage 4's `skill vs persistence` is your real evidence.\n\n## Next, in order\n\n1. **Status cell** \u2192 confirm `FINISHED`, `32 of 32`, and note the `last.ckpt` path it prints (`save_last=True` wrote one at epoch end this time, since the run completed).\n2. **Save + close wandb** \u2014 remember the filename change:\n   ```python\n   trainer.save_checkpoint(\"finetuned_32steps.ckpt\")   # NOT interrupted_33steps.ckpt\n   import wandb\n   if wandb.run is not None: wandb.run.finish()\n   ```\n3. **Stage 4.** Decide `paired` first: `paired=True` if you want the flipped-vs-upright comparison to actually work, `paired=False` (default) to stay consistent with the baseline you already computed.\n4. **Stage 4b** for the figures.",
