      "body": "Prompt is too longShort answer for the cell you pasted: **nothing new.** It needs `torch` (cell 1 already imports it) and `lit_model` (cells 5\u201310). If cell 1 and 5\u201310 have run, paste it as-is.\n\nHere's the full per-cell breakdown so you don't hit a `NameError` mid-presentation.\n\n## One cell that covers everything\n\nPaste this once, right after cell 1, and every cell I gave you will run:\n\n```python\n# --- imports for the diagnostic / eval / plot cells ---\nimport os, time, datetime as dt\nfrom uuid import uuid4\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed\n\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec\nimport sunpy.visualization.colormaps as cm          # registers sdoaia131 / hmimag colormaps\nfrom torch.utils.data._utils.collate import default_collate\n\nimport wandb\nprint(\"imports ok\")\n```\n\n`numpy as np`, `pandas as pd`, `torch`, `lightning as L` are already in cell 1 \u2014 don't re-import them, just make sure cell 1 ran.\n\n## Per cell, if you'd rather keep them local\n\n| Cell | New imports | Live objects it needs |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Recovery** (`torch.load` + `load_state_dict`) | none | `torch`, `lit_model` |\n| **`lora_B` nonzero check** | none | `lit_model` |\n| **Reload `df_baseline`** | none | `pd` |\n| **Stage 4** (`evaluate`) | none | `lit_model`, `val_data_loader`, `test_data_loader`, `cfg` |\n| **Stage 4b** (`report_and_plot`) | `matplotlib.pyplot as plt`, `matplotlib.gridspec as gridspec`, `sunpy.visualization.colormaps as cm`, `default_collate` | `cfg`, `lit_model`, `val_ds`/`test_ds` |\n| **`StepProgress`** | `time`, `datetime as dt` | `L` (cell 1) |\n| **Fixed status cell** | none | `trainer`, `train_data_loader` |\n| **Save / wandb close** | `wandb` | `trainer` |\n| **Prefetch cell** | `os`, `time`, `uuid4`, `ThreadPoolExecutor`, `as_completed` | `pd`, `cfg`, `train_ds`/`val_ds`/`test_ds` |\n\n## Two things to watch\n\n**`import sunpy.visualization.colormaps as cm` looks unused \u2014 it isn't.** Importing it is what registers `sdoaia131`, `hmimag`, etc. with matplotlib. Drop it and your `plt.get_cmap(\"sdoaia131\")` calls fail. Don't let a linter \"clean\" it.\n\n**The status cell and the save cell can't run after the kernel restart.** They reference `trainer`, which died with the kernel, and I told you to skip cell 14 in the recovery path. That's correct \u2014 those two cells are for a live run, not for recovery. Skip them; go straight from the checkpoint load to Stage 4.Let me check what your notebook actually labels \"Stage 1\" so I don't guess.",
